tom.roddy@morganstanley.com wrote:
>I love playing knights and jousting, but I hate it when my lance
>breaks.  Here's my proposal for an artifact lance:
>
>A silver lance named "Wyrmslayer"
>
>Applied: +5 to hit, +5 damage (1d6+5 vs small / 1d8+5 vs Large)
>Wielded (mounted): +5 to hit, +5 damage (1d6+5 vs small / 1d8+5 vs
>Large)
>Wielded (not mounted): 1d2 vs small & Large
>
>Specials:
>x2 damage vs Dragons
>x2 vs silver-hating monsters

You can't (currently) have something be +1d5 versus everything *and* have
it do double damage versus a specific type of target. (Also, as things
stand you can't make a weapon do double damage against silver-haters
without additional coding effort; silver-hating is not stored in the
monster data structures.)

Without additional code, there are two options for damage bonus:

* A non-zero number (n) - this translates to +1d(n) damage on each hit.
* Zero - this translates to double damage on each hit.

and three options for what the damage and to-hit bonuses apply to:

* All monsters who do not resist the type of damage used by the bonus.
* All monsters represented by a certain symbol who do not resist the
  type of damage used by the bonus.
* All monsters with a certain attribute flag who do not resist the type
  of damage used by the bonus.

Obviously, additional code could be written to support this artifact.
However, I don't think it's *interesting* enough to make the coding effort
worthwhile.  The effort that went into Magicbane was worthwhile, because
Magicbane does interesting things.

(I also think an across-the-board double-damage against all
silver-haters is too powerful a bonus...)

>15% chance (based on your to-hit roll) of cancelling a dragon.
>      "Wyrmslayer shines brilliantly!" if you can see or
>      "Wyrmslayer roars deafeningly!" if you can't
>      and "It strikes <monster>!"
>    The dragon may resist cancellation.

The only dragons against which a cancellation effect that requires a
succesful melee hit is more than marginally relevant are the Caveman
and Knight quest nemeses; dragons will *never* use their breath weapon
while in melee range of their intended target.

[jousting rules snipped]
>Unlike normal lances, Wyrmslayer is *unbreakable* and will never
>shatter from successful jousting!

This is a good attribute for an artifact lance.

I think there should be an artifact lance; I think your proposed
artifact lance is not the artifact lance that Nethack should have. (For
one thing, I think the game doesn't need another type of silver weapon,
let alone another silver artifact.)

(Oh, and your citing of SLASH'EM's "Reaper" was irrelevant to Nethack
in general.  If you meant to specifically make a proposal for SLASH'EM,
it's customary to put [S] in the subject line.)
